[SLIDE: DML Exception Management]

[CONTENT_START]
• DEFENSIVE CODING BOUNDARY: Intercept script failures before user view spaces crash.
• TRY-CATCH WRAPPER SCHEMA:
  try {
      $record = $DB->get_record('quiz', ['id' => $quizid], '*', MUST_EXIST);
  } catch (dml_missing_record_exception $e) {
      meta_log_incident($e->getMessage());
  }
• DIAGNOSTIC EXCEPTIONS: dmlreadexception highlights explicit schema validation conflicts early.
[CONTENT_END]

[NARRATIVE: Defensive coding relies on handling explicit errors. Moodle protects database interactions through validation layers. When you request rows using strict structural flags, the engine throws targeted missing-record exceptions if data isn't there, allowing you to intercept failures smoothly before they break the user interface.]
